# What the home-assistant form, booted as it ships, without a shell and
# without a config, must say on its console (make
# check-shellfree-home-assistant; test/boot; forms/demo/test/console has
# the format). With no owner, Home Assistant parks before
# home-assistant-setup or Home Assistant runs, and says why; Caddy, with
# no domain, serves plain HTTP. make check-home-assistant boots it with
# its config, and logs in.

seen    ha-needs-password  leash: \{"event":"down","service":"home-assistant","why":"config owner-password: FileNotFound"\}
unseen  caddy-down         leash: \{"event":"down","service":"caddy"
